@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

### Register
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{"email":"test@test.com","password":"password123","name":"Test User"}

### Register - duplicate email (should 409 ConflictException)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{"email":"test@test.com","password":"password123","name":"Test User"}

### Register - invalid email
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{"email":"not-an-email","password":"password123","name":"Test User"}

### Register - password too short
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{"email":"test2@test.com","password":"123","name":"Test User"}

### Login correct
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email":"test@test.com","password":"password123"}

### Login wrong password (should 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email":"test@test.com","password":"wrongpassword"}

### Login - user doesn't exist (should 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email":"nouser@test.com","password":"password123"}

### Refresh - uses cookie set by the login request above
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: refresh_token={{login.response.headers.Set-Cookie}}

### Refresh - no cookie (should 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

### Logout - uses cookie set by the login request above
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: refresh_token={{login.response.headers.Set-Cookie}}

### Logout - no cookie (should 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json

### ===== Refresh token rotation =====

### Rotation step 1 - login to start a fresh family (token A)
# @name rotationLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email":"test@test.com","password":"password123"}

### Rotation step 2 - use token A, should succeed and set a NEW cookie (token B)
# expect: 200/201, Set-Cookie header present, refresh_token value differs from token A
# @name rotationStep2
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: refresh_token={{rotationLogin.response.headers.Set-Cookie}}

### Rotation step 3 - use token B, should succeed and set a NEW cookie (token C)
# expect: 200/201, Set-Cookie header present, refresh_token value differs from token B
# @name rotationStep3
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: refresh_token={{rotationStep2.response.headers.Set-Cookie}}

### Rotation step 4 - use token C, confirms the chain keeps rotating normally
# expect: 200/201, Set-Cookie header present
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: refresh_token={{rotationStep3.response.headers.Set-Cookie}}

### ===== Token theft detection =====

### Theft step 1 - login to start a fresh family
# @name theftLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email":"test@test.com","password":"password123"}

### Theft step 2 - legit rotation, token A -> token B (attacker doesn't act yet)
# @name theftStep2
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: refresh_token={{theftLogin.response.headers.Set-Cookie}}

### Theft step 3 - REPLAY token A (already used) - simulates attacker with a stolen old token
# expect: 401 Unauthorized (token A has used = true from step 2)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: refresh_token={{theftLogin.response.headers.Set-Cookie}}

### Theft step 4 - legit user tries token B (the one issued after the legit rotation)
# expect: 401 Unauthorized - family was revoked by step 3's reuse detection,
# even though token B itself was never individually replayed
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: refresh_token={{theftStep2.response.headers.Set-Cookie}}